From: bluseliu50 <265648257+bluseliu50@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:27:25 +0800
Subject: piano: drm/msm/dpu: round up the DSC active width of DSI interfaces

With a compression ratio that is not integral (10 bpc at 8 bpp) the
truncated width leaves the interface line one clock shorter than the
DSI one, which rounds up. The interface then runs ahead of the DSI
video engine until its FIFO overflows a few hundred lines into every
frame. Round up like the DSI host and the vendor driver do.

Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/b4bbd449650407ae4e0f4ef6e31110eff9c489a3
Link: https://github.com/blu-sharky/linux-piano/commit/5c2c95fddbe9c29720b7b4e84119357358e9f0cb
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
index ba810f26ea3099106aac1783f7f6bf5e014e41a0..cfa2ad2403d6d07593d2ee16d039b59a1e8a1096 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c
@@ -133,9 +133,14 @@ static void drm_mode_to_intf_timing_params(
 		/*
 		 * TODO: replace drm_dsc_get_bpp_int with logic to handle
 		 * fractional part if there is fraction
+		 *
+		 * Round up like the DSI host does for its active width: with
+		 * e.g. 10 bpc at 8 bpp the ratio is not integral, and a line
+		 * one clock shorter than the DSI one makes the interface run
+		 * ahead of the DSI video engine until its FIFO overflows.
 		 */
-		timing->width = timing->width * drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc) /
-				(dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
+		timing->width = DIV_ROUND_UP(timing->width * drm_dsc_get_bpp_int(dsc),
+					     dsc->bits_per_component * 3);
 		timing->xres = timing->width;
 		timing->dce_bytes_per_line = msm_dsc_get_bytes_per_line(dsc);
 	}
